Fires on a fresh tree or when inputs change. Defines how the campaign's inputs are obtained/generated
and split, so the data is reproducible and the splits stay fixed.

> **Never regenerate or overwrite inputs on an unconfirmed diagnosis.** Inputs are load-bearing and
> overwriting them is usually irreversible. Before acting on the theory that the data is wrong, the diagnosis
> must reach **CONFIRMED via the highest-authority artifact** — read the actual data-prep / pipeline source,
> don't act on a derived statistic or a plausible correlation. (A real session nearly overwrote a *correct*
> dataset on an INFERRED diagnosis; reading the normalization source reversed it.) Gating a destructive
> action to the user on a below-CONFIRMED diagnosis makes the human your only backstop — confirm first.

